---
description: Vue 3 + TypeScript frontend conventions
globs: pages/**/*.{ts,vue,mts,cts}
alwaysApply: false
---

- Vue 3 Composition API in TypeScript. Component pattern: `.setup.ts` (logic, exports a `useFoo()` composable) + `.vue` (template that calls it). Each `.setup.ts` has a colocated `.spec.ts`.
- Features under `pages/src/features/`: `auth`, `barcode`, `dashboard`, `home`, `mobile-id`, `profile`. Each feature owns its own `api/`, components, and feature-local composables.
- Shared API layer (`pages/src/shared/api/`): only `client.ts`, `axios.ts`, `csrf.ts`. Per-feature API calls live alongside the feature — e.g. `features/auth/api/authApi.ts` for login/register/logout/user_info, `features/auth/api/tokenRefresh.ts` for JWT auto-refresh.
- Shared utils (`pages/src/shared/utils/`): `cookie.ts`, `profileUtils.ts`, `common/dateUtils.ts`. There is no `encryption.ts`, `webauthn.ts`, or `tokenRefresh.ts` here — those used to exist and were intentionally removed.
- Composables (`pages/src/shared/composables/`): `api/` → `useLoading`, `useServerWakeup`; `device/` → `useCameraPermission`, `useScannerDetection`; `persistence/` → `useAutoSave`. There is no barrel `index.ts` — import full paths like `@shared/composables/api/useLoading`.
- Path aliases (defined in `pages/path-aliases.json`, applied via `pages/alias.config.mjs`): `@`, `@app`, `@auth`, `@barcode`, `@dashboard`, `@home`, `@mobile-id`, `@profile`, `@shared`. Use them — don't write deep relative paths.
- Auth flow: SPA POSTs `{ username, password }` plaintext over HTTPS to `/authn/login/`. Backend issues JWT cookies. There is no client-side RSA encryption and no WebAuthn/passkey UI today, even though the backend exposes those endpoints.
- Build runs typecheck first: `yarn build` = `yarn typecheck && vite build`. Run `yarn typecheck` standalone before committing.
- Format/lint: `yarn format` (Prettier write), `yarn lint` (ESLint on `src/`).
- Yarn 1.x only — locked via `packageManager` in `package.json`.
